program Kinship.
note Family relations derived by the kernel (Datalog) from parent(P, C) facts. A model only has to
note extract the parent facts from a story; every multi-hop relation is then computed, not guessed.

rule child(C, P) if parent(P, C).
rule ancestor(A, D) if parent(A, D).
rule ancestor(A, D) if parent(A, X) and ancestor(X, D).
rule descendant(D, A) if ancestor(A, D).
rule sibling(X, Y) if parent(P, X) and parent(P, Y) and X != Y.
rule grandparent(G, C) if parent(G, P) and parent(P, C).
rule cousin(X, Y) if parent(PX, X) and parent(PY, Y) and sibling(PX, PY).

test "three generations" do
  fact parent(ada, ben), parent(ada, cy), parent(ben, dee), parent(cy, eli).
  assert holds ancestor(ada, dee).
  assert holds grandparent(ada, eli).
  assert holds cousin(dee, eli).
  assert holds sibling(ben, cy).
  assert not (holds sibling(ben, ben)).
end.
